WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.760
You go to change a line,

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.320
but its reason lives in a handbook,

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:06.580
so the code gets hard to change.

4
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:11.000
That's why my code documentation gives each answer one of three homes.

5
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.040
A comment holds local reasoning,

6
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:16.633
like the stable ordering a later edit could quietly break.

7
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:20.353
A docstring states what a function accepts or returns,

8
00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:23.767
so the generated reference stays beside the code.

9
00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:29.367
But generated pages can't reliably say what to do when a valid request fails,

10
00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.333
so that goes in a guide.

11
00:00:31.333 --> 00:00:34.613
So I'd ask what the reader needs at that moment,

12
00:00:34.613 --> 00:00:37.053
because that decides where it belongs.
